# SoulsSMP — Project Guide

THIS GUIDE IS OLD SO SOME STUFF MIGHT BE UPDATED SO YOU STILL HAVE TO SCAN THE FILES!

This is a custom Minecraft Paper/Spigot plugin (Java, Gradle project). Read this fully before touching any code — it explains the concept, what's already built, how it's structured, and the conventions to follow.

## The Core Concept

Every player gets bound to one of several unique **Souls**, each a different force of existence. A Soul grants:
- A **passive trait** that's always active
- **Mana-based abilities** (2 regular abilities + 1 Ultimate)
- Eventually, a **weapon Awakening** (binding the Soul into a custom weapon — not built yet)
- Progression through a **Favor** system (-5 to +5) tied to quests/kills/relics — not built yet
- A **Resurrection** system: reaching +5 Favor lets you sacrifice your current Soul to become stronger, reroll into a new Soul, gain more max mana, and get permanent buffs (halo, wings). Dying after resurrecting resets Favor to -1 instead of 0, but you keep resurrection status until you die again. — not built yet
- **Rituals**: physical world locations (ritual plates) required to Awaken weapons or Resurrect. — not built yet

Long-term structure: players climb a Soul Ranking (First Life → Awakened → Reborn → Ascended → Eternal Soul → GOD) through repeated resurrections, each time becoming more unique.

Only **2 of a planned 8 souls** are built right now: **Void** and **Blood**. The rest are undesigned.

## What's Fully Built and Working

### Core framework
- `SoulManager` — assigns/reads a player's `SoulType` enum (currently `VOID`, `BLOOD`)
- `PlayerData` / `PlayerDataManager` — holds soul, mana, maxMana, favor, resurrectionCount, awakened flag. **Persists to disk** as YAML at `plugins/SoulsSMP/playerdata/<uuid>.yml`, loaded on join / saved on quit and plugin disable.
- `ManaManager` — get/set/spend/add mana, respects Creative mode (infinite) and Silence (see below)
- `ManaTask` — passive regen, +5 mana every 5 seconds (reads as a satisfying chunky tick, not a slow crawl). Skips silenced players entirely.
- `AbilityManager` — central registry of all abilities. Enforces cooldowns, enforces that an ability's `requiredSoul` matches the caster's actual bound soul, skips cooldowns/mana costs in Creative mode.
- `Ability` (abstract base class) — every ability has a type, display name, mana cost, cooldown, and a `requiredSoul`. `execute()` returns boolean: true = counted as a real use (start cooldown), false = nothing happened (failed cast, or a multi-phase ability still charging).

### HUD (all via `HudTask`, runs 5x/second)
- **Mana**: boss bar at top of screen, purple, shows current/max (or ∞ in Creative)
- **Ultimate**: boss bar, shows cooldown countdown or "READY (Sneak+F)". Label and color swap automatically based on which soul/mode the player is in (e.g. Blood shows "Blood Hands" above 5 hearts, "Puncture" at/below 5 hearts)
- **Two regular abilities**: shown in the action bar (text just above hotbar), each ability's mana cost is prefixed like `(40) Curse`, doubled and shown correctly if the caster is Silenced. Cooldown shown as a 10-segment colored bar, or a live "Marked (Xs)" / stack-counter display for abilities that don't use traditional cooldowns (Abyss Mark, Hemorrhage).
- Boss bars are created on join, removed on quit (`HudJoinQuitListener` + `HudManager`)

### Commands
- `/soul` — shows your own soul, mana, favor, resurrections, awakened status
- `/soul info` — lists all souls; `/soul info <name>` shows full ability breakdown for that soul
- `/soul ability1` and `/soul ability2` — **generic slot-based activation**, NOT named per-soul. Slot 1/2 map to whichever 2 abilities belong to your current soul (Void: Void Step / Abyss Mark. Blood: Curse / Hemorrhage). This was changed from the old `/soul ability <name>` syntax — always use ability1/ability2 going forward for any new soul.
- `/soultest <void|blood>` — dev/testing only, force-assigns a soul + sets mana to 100/100. `/soultest mana <amount>` sets mana directly. Not part of real progression — will eventually be replaced by Rituals.
- Ultimates are triggered by **Sneak + F** (`PlayerSwapHandItemsEvent`, cancelled so it doesn't actually swap items), NOT a command. `UltimateTriggerListener` checks the player's soul and fires the right ultimate.
- Tab-completion exists for both `/soul` and `/soultest` via dedicated `TabCompleter` classes — remember to update these if new subcommands/abilities are added.

### Creative Mode rules (apply to every soul)
- Infinite mana (never depletes, bar always shows full/∞)
- No cooldowns on any ability
- Costs that would sacrifice HP (like Blood Hands) are waived entirely in Creative

